VendorSync::best is a raw pointer into available_profiles, set during
sort_available() and never cleared. PresetUpdater::reload_all_vendors()
calls load_unused_vendors() multiple times — once for the user's
~/.config/SuperSlicer/vendor/ entries (a single emplace_back + sort sets
best=&[0]), then again for matching profiles copied from the resources
tree into ~/.config/SuperSlicer/cache/vendor/. The second call does
another emplace_back on the same VendorSync's vector, which may
reallocate, freeing the buffer that `best` still points at. The first
loop in sort_available() then reads best->config_version → SIGSEGV.

Fix: reset best to nullptr at the top of sort_available(). The final
loop already recomputes it.

--- a/src/slic3r/Utils/PresetUpdater.cpp
+++ b/src/slic3r/Utils/PresetUpdater.cpp
@@ -609,6 +609,10 @@ bool VendorSync::parse_tags(const std::string &json) {
 }

 void VendorSync::sort_available() {
+    // Reset cached pointer into available_profiles before recomputing: any
+    // prior emplace_back may have reallocated the vector, leaving `best`
+    // dangling, and the loop below would dereference it.
+    best = nullptr;
     if (available_profiles.empty()) {
         return;
     }
